                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 3]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Reuter’s Agency Report in the “Peking &amp; Tientsin
                        Times” July 29, 1920</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-28"><hi rendition="#italic">July 28</hi>[, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">1920</hi>]</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Diplomatic Corps held a Meeting to-day, and discussed the question of
                    refugees in the Legation Quarter, but did not reach any decision. It is
                    understood that the British, American, and French Ministers are reminding their
                    nationals in the Quarter that in accordance with the Protocol, Chinese cannot
                    reside within the Legation Quarter, and if they are at present harbouring any
                    Chinese, they must be turned out within forty-eight hours. This, of course, does
                    not apply to the Legations.</p>
            </div>
